11. What is AWS API rate limit error ?
-- Definition
AWS API rate limit error happens when too many API requests are sent in short time

-- Common scenarios
✅ Terraform apply 🔥
✅ Auto Scaling
✅ Lambda / API Gateway
✅ CloudFormation

-- Error reason
✅ Too many parallel requests
✅ Large infrastructure creation
✅ AWS throttling limits

-- How to fix
✅ Reduce parallelism
terraform apply -parallelism=2
✅ Target specific resources (temporary use)
terraform apply -target=module.vpc
✅ Optimize Terraform code
✅ Add retry logic (provider handles some retries)
✅ Request AWS quota increase

-- Best Practice
✅ Keep parallelism balanced (default = 10)
✅ Use modules for structured deploy
✅ Avoid unnecessary resource recreation
✅ Monitor API usage

12. What is terraform drift ? 
Terraform drift happens when real infrastructure changes outside Terraform, so it no longer matches the Terraform state file

-- Reason of drift 
  ✅ Manual changes (AWS Console)
  ✅ Someone runs CLI (aws cli)
  ✅ Other automation tools
  ✅ Team members modifying infra

-- How to detect drift
   terraform plan 
   terraform refresh

-- How to fix
   Terraform apply                                 -- wil match the code
   update terraform code & terraform apply         -- this will  match the code & real infra
   terraform import aws_instance.web i-123456      -- import the changes into the code

-- Best Practice
   ✅ Always use Terraform for changes
   ✅ Restrict manual access
   ✅ Use remote state (S3)
   ✅ Use CI/CD pipelines to check drift
   ✅ Enable audit logs

13. Resource removed from code but still exist in cloud, How to fix ?
If a resource is removed from Terraform code but still exists in the cloud, 
Terraform will plan to destroy it unless it is removed from the state using terraform state rm.
terraform state rm module.rds.aws_db_instance.db

Action                               Result
Remove from code + apply             resource deleted 
Remove from state                    resource kept 
Add back in code                     no deletion 

14. Provider/API bahviour changed after the upgrade , how to fix ?
Pin Provider Version In versions.tf
Check Provider Changelog
Use .terraform.lock.hcl          module dependencies stored
Downgrade Provider (Quick Fix)  terraform init -upgrade=false
Update code

15. What is circular dependencies b/w module and how to fix it ?
Circular dependency occurs when two modules or resources depend on each other, creating a loop that Terraform cannot resolve and 
Terraform gets stuck: Which one to create first?

Why Circular Dependency Happens
-- Wrong module design
-- Passing outputs incorrectly
-- Mutual dependency between modules
-- Tight coupling

How to fix 
-- Break the Dependency-Fix design so dependency is one direction only
-- Use Linear Flow Design-VPC → SG → EC2 ✅
-- Use Separate Resources- VPC module → only creates VPC and SG module → only uses VPC ID
-- Modules should be:
   ✅ Independent  
   ✅ Reusable  
   ✅ loosely coupled

16. What happens when AWS quota limits hits ?
When AWS quota limits are exceeded, API requests fail and Terraform cannot create resources, leading to partial or failed deployment

Why Quota Limit Happens
-- Creating more resources than allowed
-- Default AWS limits are low
-- High parallel resource creation
-- Multiple users/tools using same account
-- Burst API requests

How to Fix
-- Increase quota in AWS Service Quotas ✅
-- Reduce number of resources ✅
-- Reduce parallelism (-parallelism) ✅
-- Split deployment into smaller steps ✅

17. What to do when remote backend access is lost?
Remote backend access loss happens when Terraform cannot access state stored remotely (S3, Azure Blob, etc.), so Terraform operations fail
Terraform gets error: state cannot be read or updated

 Why It Happens
-- S3 bucket / storage account not accessible
-- IAM permission issue ❌
-- Network issue ❌
-- Wrong backend configuration ❌
-- State file deleted or corrupted ❌

How to Fix
-- Restore backend access (permissions/network) ✅
-- Fix IAM roles/credentials ✅
-- Correct backend configuration ✅
-- Restore state file from backup ✅
-- Reconfigure backend using terraform init -reconfigure ✅
-- use versioning


